    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d25-a1">

                <pb facs="0159" n="25" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg25"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 90.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Newton to Mr.
                            Rives.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >St. Paul de Loanda</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-09-30"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 30,
                        1887</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 33.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose copy of a
                    petition drawn up by the Rev. A. Billington, of the American Baptist Missionary
                    Union at Stanley Pool, and to ask for instructions with reference to the same. I
                    doubt if any papers granted by me would be recognized by the Congo Free State,
                    as I am not recoguized as consul for that district.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robt. S. Newton</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Vice-Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
